title: Phase 1 SHIPPED — graph-slice projector (render-by-projection) standalone primitive
summary: 'Built + verified + reviewed Phase 1 of the symbol-graph-as-discourse-substrate arc: a standalone `paradigm graph slice <symbol>` CLI command + paradigm_graph_slice MCP tool that project a bounded, deterministic slice of the REAL symbol graph and emit it as a renderable mermaid block (renders today) or a conductor-visual `graph` envelope (Phase-2 cockpit target). Shared projector lives in @a-company/premise-core (graph-slice.ts). Key correctness fix during the build: first cut sourced edges from scan-index `related[]` + the stale flow-index.json (only 7 flows, missing all conductor flows) and rendered major components BARE; re-based onto the LIVE parse (aggregateFromDirectory + buildSymbolIndex + getReferencesTo/getReferencesFrom + flow membership) — the exact path the ripple CLI uses — so #cockpit-view now correctly shows its $fleet-switch flow edge + real dependents. Reviewer APPROVED (0 blockers); 18 tests green; all three packages build. Render-by-projection keystone proven on screen.'
