  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/index.ts
learnings:
  - The authoritative rich edge source is the LIVE parse (aggregateFromDirectory + buildSymbolIndex + getReferencesTo/getReferencesFrom + findFlowMembership) used by the ripple CLI — NOT scan-index.json `related[]` (only 32% of components have any) and NOT flow-index.json (stale; held only 7 flows, missing every conductor flow). Anything needing rich grounded graph edges should re-use ripple's live-index path, not the serialized indices.
  - 'Sourcing from the live parse sidesteps the scan-index.json determinism wart entirely: the projector sorts its own topology (nodes by id, edges by source+target+kind) so output is byte-identical across runs; freshness.generatedAt is an intentionally-live timestamp (stale=false), the only inter-run variance.'
  - 'Perf note: aggregateFromDirectory re-parses the whole project per call (the cost ripple already pays) — fine for a CLI invocation, but the MCP/cockpit default-on-every-turn path will want a cached index later.'
